                                <h4 class="title-two">The question that actually matters</h4>
                                <p>The debate about crypto&rsquo;s future is mostly settled &mdash; digital assets are becoming part of the global financial system, and regulation is maturing rather than disappearing. The open question is different. It is not whether crypto will go global. It is whether you are positioned globally. For the past decade the edge came from conviction &mdash; the right coin, the right cycle. Over the next decade I suspect it will come from somewhere less obvious: not from what you hold, but from where, and how, and under whose rules you hold it.</p>

